      "writtenOn": "2023-07-12T15:33:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`rendererOutset` can be infinite in AnalyticRRectRenderStep when the localToDevice matrix is really degenerate or if the bounding box would have points clipped behind the w\u003d0 plane.\n\nWe should check for that before applying the outset to `transformedShapeBounds`. I think what makes sense when an infinite outset is returned, is to skip over lines 1141 to 1179 and set `transformedShapeBounds` and `drawBounds` to `deviceBounds`, as well as setting `styledShape` and `shapeInDeviceSpace` like we do in the if true condition at line 1170.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1140,
        "startChar": 10,
        "endLine": 1140,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "50f40605be4b53c53179fc55dcffa148c3dca1d4",
